{"beat_id": "S016_B062", "speaker_id": "maevra", "text": "Not tonight.", "left": {}, "right": {}, "active_side": "none", "advance_mode": "manual", "cues": {"pause_ms": 80, "interrupt": false, "implementation_flags": ["IN_WORLD_DIALOGUE"], "source_section": "B009 — USEFUL", "source_speaker_label": "MAEVRA", "staging": "Maevra understands the distinction."}},
{"beat_id": "S016_B063", "speaker_id": "torren", "text": "Wasn’t suggesting tonight.", "left": {}, "right": {}, "active_side": "none", "advance_mode": "manual", "cues": {"pause_ms": 80, "interrupt": false, "implementation_flags": ["IN_WORLD_DIALOGUE"], "source_section": "B009 — USEFUL", "source_speaker_label": "TORREN", "staging_after": "That’s it. No Hunt exposition. No monster name spoken. No quest-board cutscene."}},
{"beat_id": "S016_B064", "speaker_id": "", "text": "", "left": {}, "right": {}, "active_side": "none", "advance_mode": "manual", "cues": {"pause_ms": 120, "staging": "> **HUNT #2 — TRANSFER EXECUTIONER: UNLOCKED / ACCESSIBLE AFTER S016**\n\nThe earlier barred prisoner-transfer branch is now open because the Bastion control state changed during S015/S016.\n\nThe player can return later through the shortened Bastion/Dunmere access route rather than replaying the entire Chapter 2 dungeon.\n\nCheap implementation: reuse existing Prisoner Galleries / transfer-spine assets; switch the barred gate to its open state; use existing route geometry; place the Hunt encounter in the established branch; no bespoke Hunt-opening cinematic and no mandatory dialogue scene.\n\nThe Hunt remains optional. The party does not turn around and do it during the evacuation.", "interrupt": false, "implementation_flags": ["SOURCE_STAGING"], "source_section": "CHAPTER 2 HUNT WORLD-STATE CHANGE"}},
{"beat_id": "S016_B065", "speaker_id": "", "text": "", "left": {}, "right": {}, "active_side": "none", "advance_mode": "manual", "cues": {"pause_ms": 120, "staging": "Same Dunmere staging background. Static composition.\n\nForeground: an evacuee receives water. Midground: the man waiting for his brother watches the Causeway entrance. A few silhouettes suggest continuing activity. The protagonists are present but aren’t posed as the center of the scene.\n\nNo dialogue. Fade.\n\n> **END S016. Chapter 2 mandatory story complete.**\n\nAvailable afterward: C06 — Three People Who Know Each Other Now; C07 — Bad Dreams, No Questions; Hunt #2 — Transfer Executioner. C06 and C07 remain order-independent. The Hunt remains optional and can be returned to rather than being forced into the chapter-ending evacuation.", "interrupt": false, "implementation_flags": ["SOURCE_STAGING"], "source_section": "B010 — END IMAGE"}},
{"beat_id": "S016_B066", "speaker_id": "", "text": "", "left": {}, "right": {}, "active_side": "none", "advance_mode": "manual", "cues": {"pause_ms": 120, "staging": "Exactly one mandatory authored combat encounter: Hold the Junction. No second rearguard battle.\n\nNo combat occurs after the final extraction threshold.\n\nRhazek survives and remains withdrawn from S015.\n\nThe missing-brother thread stays unresolved.\n\nThe evacuation is represented cheaply through portraits, offscreen sound, a handful of sprites, silhouettes, state swaps, and reused spaces rather than crowd choreography.\n\nHunt #2 — Transfer Executioner unlocks through the west-branch gate state change but is not forced into S016.", "interrupt": false, "implementation_flags": ["SOURCE_STAGING", "NO_COMBAT_AFTER_THIS_BEAT", "STORY_CHAPTER_02_COMPLETE", "UNLOCK_C06_THREE_PEOPLE_WHO_KNOW_EACH_OTHER_NOW", "UNLOCK_C07_BAD_DREAMS_NO_QUESTIONS", "UNLOCK_HUNT_02_TRANSFER_EXECUTIONER", "DO_NOT_AUTO_SKIP_CHARACTER_LIFE_SCENES"], "source_section": "S016 — LOCKED CONTINUITY NOTES"}}
]
